Every work card MUST conform to this file. Where a work card and this file
disagree, this file wins. Do not rename types, change signatures, or move
files without being told to.

## 0. Repository layout

```
D:\BenchRuns\XL-B-01\
  BatchRenameStudio.sln
  src\BatchRenameStudio\BatchRenameStudio.csproj
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Program.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Cli\ConsoleBridge.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Cli\HeadlessRunner.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\Model\ApplyTo.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\Model\SortMode.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\Model\StepContext.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\Model\NameState.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\Model\RuleStep.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\Model\RuleSet.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\NameRules.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\Results.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\JsonOutput.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\StepFactory.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\Steps\*.cs          (15 files)
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\RulesJson.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\FileScanner.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\RenameEngine.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\RenameExecutor.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Core\UndoJournal.cs
  src\BatchRenameStudio\Ui\*.cs
  docs\, README.md
```

Root namespace: `BatchRenameStudio`. Sub-namespaces mirror folders
(`BatchRenameStudio.Core`, `BatchRenameStudio.Core.Model`,
`BatchRenameStudio.Core.Steps`, `BatchRenameStudio.Cli`,
`BatchRenameStudio.Ui`).

Project settings: `net8.0-windows`, `OutputType=WinExe`, `UseWindowsForms=true`,
`Nullable=enable`, `ImplicitUsings=enable`, `AssemblyName=BatchRenameStudio`,
`LangVersion=latest`, `InvariantGlobalization=false`.
No PackageReference of any kind. No `global.json`.

Code and code comments are English. Only user-visible GUI strings are
Traditional Chinese.

## 1. Model types (owned by WC-A)

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core.Model;

public enum ApplyTo { Name, NameAndExtension }
public enum SortMode { Name, Created, Modified }

/// Per-file, per-run immutable context handed to every step.
public sealed class StepContext
{
    public int Index { get; }            // 0-based position in processing order
    public string OriginalName { get; }  // full original file name
    public string OriginalBase { get; }  // rule 2 base of OriginalName
    public string OriginalExt { get; }   // rule 2 ext of OriginalName, no dot
    public ApplyTo ApplyTo { get; }
    public StepContext(int index, string originalName, string originalBase,
                       string originalExt, ApplyTo applyTo);
}

/// Mutable state threaded through the step chain for one file.
public sealed class NameState
{
    /// The "target string" of the spec: base under ApplyTo.Name,
    /// the whole file name under ApplyTo.NameAndExtension.
    public string Target { get; set; } = "";
    /// Current extension (no dot). Only meaningful under ApplyTo.Name;
    /// under ApplyTo.NameAndExtension it stays "" and is never read.
    public string Ext { get; set; } = "";
}

public abstract class RuleStep
{
    /// JSON "op" value, e.g. "replace".
    public abstract string Op { get; }

    /// GUI-only. Never serialized. Disabled steps are dropped before the
    /// engine runs, so they never appear in a trace.
    [Browsable(false)] public bool Enabled { get; set; } = true;

    /// Mutates state. MUST NOT throw for any input.
    public abstract void Apply(StepContext ctx, NameState state);

    /// Reads this step's own properties from its JSON object.
    /// Missing/invalid members fall back to the documented default.
    /// MUST NOT throw.
    public abstract void ReadJson(JsonElement element);

    /// Writes this step's own properties. The caller has already written
    /// StartObject and the "op" property.
    public abstract void WriteJson(Utf8JsonWriter writer);

    /// One-line Traditional-Chinese summary for the GUI rule list.
    public abstract string Describe();
}

public sealed class RuleSet
{
    public ApplyTo ApplyTo { get; set; } = ApplyTo.Name;
    public SortMode Sort { get; set; } = SortMode.Name;
    public List<RuleStep> Steps { get; } = new();
}
```

## 2. NameRules (owned by WC-A)

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core;

public static class NameRules
{
    /// Spec rule 2. dot = LAST '.' index; dot > 0 => base=[0,dot), ext=(dot,end];
    /// otherwise base = whole name, ext = "".
    public static (string Base, string Ext) Split(string name);

    /// Spec rule 6. ext=="" ? baseName : baseName + "." + ext
    public static string Join(string baseName, string ext);

    /// Spec rule 7 first bullet. Returns true and a short reason when invalid.
    public static bool IsInvalid(string proposedName, out string reason);

    public static readonly char[] IllegalChars =
        { '<', '>', ':', '"', '/', '\\', '|', '?', '*' };
    public static bool IsReservedBase(string baseName);   // CON/PRN/AUX/NUL/COM1-9/LPT1-9
}
```

`IsInvalid` order of checks (reason strings are free text, keep them short and
English-free is not required — use Traditional Chinese):
1. `proposedName.Length == 0` → "名稱為空"
2. `proposedName.Length > 255` → "長度超過 255"  (Length = `string.Length`)
3. contains any `IllegalChars` → "含非法字元 X"
4. any `c < '\u0020'` → "含控制字元"
5. `IsReservedBase(Split(proposedName).Base)` → "保留裝置名稱"

## 3. Results (owned by WC-A)

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core;

public static class PlanStatus   // exact JSON strings
{
    public const string Ok = "ok";
    public const string Collision = "collision";
    public const string Unchanged = "unchanged";
    public const string Invalid = "invalid";
}

public sealed class PlanItem
{
    public string Original { get; set; } = "";
    public string Proposed { get; set; } = "";
    public string Status   { get; set; } = PlanStatus.Ok;
    public string Reason   { get; set; } = "";
}

public sealed class TraceStep
{
    public int Index { get; set; }
    public string Op { get; set; } = "";
    public string Before { get; set; } = "";
    public string After { get; set; } = "";
}

public sealed class TraceFile
{
    public string Original { get; set; } = "";
    public List<TraceStep> Steps { get; } = new();
    public string Proposed { get; set; } = "";
    public string Status { get; set; } = PlanStatus.Ok;
}

public sealed class PlanSummary
{
    public int Total, Ok, Collision, Unchanged, Invalid;
}

/// One engine pass produces BOTH outputs, so --plan and --explain can never
/// disagree. Items[i] and Files[i] describe the same file.
public sealed class EngineResult
{
    public List<PlanItem> Items { get; } = new();
    public List<TraceFile> Files { get; } = new();
    public PlanSummary Summary { get; set; } = new();
}
```

## 4. JsonOutput (owned by WC-A)

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core;

public static class JsonOutput
{
    public static byte[] PlanBytes(EngineResult r);
    public static byte[] TraceBytes(EngineResult r);
    /// Creates the parent directory if needed, writes bytes verbatim.
    public static void WriteFile(string path, byte[] bytes);
}
```

Rules: build the JSON with `Utf8JsonWriter` over an `ArrayBufferWriter<byte>`
using `new JsonWriterOptions { Indented = true, Encoder =
JavaScriptEncoder.UnsafeRelaxedJsonEscaping }`. `File.WriteAllBytes` — this
guarantees UTF-8 **without BOM**. Property names and shapes exactly as the
task spec (`schemaVersion` = 1). `summary` keys: `total, ok, collision,
unchanged, invalid`.

## 5. StepFactory (stub in WC-A, real in WC-B)

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core;

public static class StepFactory
{
    /// Op ids in GUI menu order. Length 14.
    public static IReadOnlyList<string> AllOps { get; }
    /// Traditional-Chinese display name for an op id (for the GUI).
    public static string DisplayName(string op);
    /// Never returns null. Unknown op => UnknownStep (a no-op that keeps
    /// its op id and raw JSON so traces and round-trips stay faithful).
    public static RuleStep Create(string op);
}
```

## 6. Engine (owned by WC-C)

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core;

public static class FileScanner
{
    /// Regular files directly inside dir, non-recursive, directories excluded,
    /// sorted per spec rule 5. Throws DirectoryNotFoundException if missing.
    public static List<FileInfo> Scan(string dir, SortMode sort);
}

public static class RenameEngine
{
    public static EngineResult Run(string dir, RuleSet rules);
    /// Same, for a caller that already scanned (GUI reuse).
    public static EngineResult Run(IReadOnlyList<string> fileNames, RuleSet rules);
}

public static class RulesJson
{
    public static RuleSet Parse(string json);          // throws JsonException on malformed JSON
    public static RuleSet Load(string path);
    public static string Serialize(RuleSet rules);     // indented, round-trips
    public static void Save(string path, RuleSet rules);
}
```

## 7. CLI (stub in WC-A, real in WC-C)

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Cli;

public static class ConsoleBridge { public static void EnsureConsole(); }
public static class HeadlessRunner { public static int Run(string[] args); }
```

`Program.Main` (WC-A, final):

```csharp
[STAThread]
static int Main(string[] args)
{
    if (args.Length > 0 && (args[0] == "--plan" || args[0] == "--explain"))
    {
        ConsoleBridge.EnsureConsole();
        return HeadlessRunner.Run(args);
    }
    ApplicationConfiguration.Initialize();
    Application.Run(new BatchRenameStudio.Ui.MainForm());
    return 0;
}
```

## 8. Spec restatement the implementer must obey

The 14 operations, the status rules, the split/join rules and the ordering
rules are restated verbatim in WC-B and WC-C. They are the product
requirement; never "improve" them.

